The original parabola is $y = x^2 - 2x + 4$.

When translated $p$ units right and $q$ units down, we replace $x$ with $(x-p)$ and subtract $q$:
$$y = (x-p)^2 - 2(x-p) + 4 - q$$

Expanding:
$$y = x^2 - 2px + p^2 - 2x + 2p + 4 - q$$
$$y = x^2 - (2p+2)x + (p^2 + 2p + 4 - q)$$

The new parabola has $x$-intercepts at 3 and 5, so it can be written as:
$$y = (x-3)(x-5) = x^2 - 8x + 15$$

Comparing coefficients:
- Coefficient of $x$: $-(2p+2) = -8$, so $2p + 2 = 8$, giving $p = 3$ ✓
- Constant term: $p^2 + 2p + 4 - q = 15$

With $p = 3$:
$$9 + 6 + 4 - q = 15$$
$$19 - q = 15$$
$$q = 4$$ ✓

